1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,960
Here is the iron thiocyanate
tube from earlier,

2
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:05,680
settled at ten units of Fe³⁺,

3
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:08,160
ten of thiocyanate and ten of the red

4
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:08,880
ion.

5
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:11,520
We add more iron, and it settles again,

6
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:14,040
at fifteen, eight and twelve.

7
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:16,320
Every amount has changed.

8
00:00:16,440 --> 00:00:18,160
Yet one thing has not.

9
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:20,480
Take the red ion, and divide by the

10
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:22,680
iron times the thiocyanate.

11
00:00:23,040 --> 00:00:26,000
Ten over ten times ten is a tenth.

12
00:00:26,080 --> 00:00:28,800
Twelve over fifteen times eight is also a

13
00:00:28,880 --> 00:00:29,920
tenth.

14
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,159
So what is this ratio, why does it

15
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:34,080
stay put, and how do we write it

16
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:35,360
for any reaction?

17
00:00:36,567 --> 00:00:38,006
First, some notation.

18
00:00:38,087 --> 00:00:42,006
Square brackets around a species
mean its concentration,

19
00:00:42,087 --> 00:00:44,886
its amount per litre, in moles per litre.

20
00:00:45,367 --> 00:00:47,526
So the red ion in brackets, over the

21
00:00:47,687 --> 00:00:50,566
iron times the thiocyanate
in brackets, is our

22
00:00:50,647 --> 00:00:51,286
ratio.

23
00:00:51,847 --> 00:00:54,006
For any settled mixture
of this reaction at

24
00:00:54,087 --> 00:00:56,486
one temperature, it comes out the same, a

25
00:00:56,567 --> 00:00:57,926
tenth in both of ours.

26
00:00:58,567 --> 00:01:00,966
Chemists give this fixed value a name, the

27
00:01:01,127 --> 00:01:05,366
equilibrium constant, K, also written Keq.

28
00:01:06,567 --> 00:01:09,126
Here is the rule for
any balanced equation,

29
00:01:09,207 --> 00:01:09,766
as written.

30
00:01:10,247 --> 00:01:13,526
Products go on top,
reactants underneath, and each

31
00:01:13,607 --> 00:01:15,846
concentration is raised
to the power of its

32
00:01:15,927 --> 00:01:16,646
coefficient.

33
00:01:17,287 --> 00:01:19,126
Let us test the power on the hydrogen

34
00:01:19,207 --> 00:01:22,406
iodide tube from the catalyst
video, hydrogen plus

35
00:01:22,487 --> 00:01:25,126
iodine making two hydrogen iodide.

36
00:01:25,687 --> 00:01:29,366
Settled, it holds two,
two and fourteen, and

37
00:01:29,487 --> 00:01:31,926
fourteen squared over two times two is a

38
00:01:32,007 --> 00:01:35,046
hundred and ninety-six
over four, forty-nine.

39
00:01:35,127 --> 00:01:37,206
A tube that started with more iodine than

40
00:01:37,287 --> 00:01:40,966
hydrogen settles at two,
eight and twenty-eight, and

41
00:01:41,047 --> 00:01:43,766
twenty-eight squared over
two times eight is seven

42
00:01:43,847 --> 00:01:47,206
hundred and eighty-four over
sixteen, forty-nine again.

43
00:01:47,447 --> 00:01:49,286
Leave the power off and you get three

44
00:01:49,367 --> 00:01:52,086
and a half, then one point seven five,

45
00:01:52,167 --> 00:01:54,326
so the ratio no longer stays put.

46
00:01:55,534 --> 00:01:58,573
Let us write an equilibrium
expression, the ratio

47
00:01:58,654 --> 00:02:01,693
for one equation, from
scratch, using the cobalt

48
00:02:01,774 --> 00:02:02,733
tube.

49
00:02:02,814 --> 00:02:05,853
The pink cobalt water
ion and chloride ions

50
00:02:05,934 --> 00:02:09,213
make the blue cobalt
chloride ion and water.

51
00:02:09,414 --> 00:02:10,973
First, the states.

52
00:02:11,214 --> 00:02:14,573
Species in solution have
concentrations that change, so

53
00:02:14,654 --> 00:02:15,773
they go in.

54
00:02:15,854 --> 00:02:18,413
The water is a liquid, the solvent, so

55
00:02:18,494 --> 00:02:19,693
it stays out.

56
00:02:19,894 --> 00:02:22,573
Second, products over reactants.

57
00:02:22,774 --> 00:02:25,373
Third, each concentration
to the power of its

58
00:02:25,454 --> 00:02:28,653
coefficient, so chloride,
with a four in front,

59
00:02:28,734 --> 00:02:30,813
is raised to the fourth power.

60
00:02:30,854 --> 00:02:33,293
The square brackets go
around the whole ion,

61
00:02:33,374 --> 00:02:35,613
including its own brackets and charge.

62
00:02:36,834 --> 00:02:39,393
Why leave out the solvent, or a solid?

63
00:02:39,874 --> 00:02:42,593
Their concentration does not
change while the reaction

64
00:02:42,674 --> 00:02:44,993
runs, so they can never make the ratio

65
00:02:45,074 --> 00:02:47,873
move, and K already includes them.

66
00:02:48,274 --> 00:02:50,033
We met this with carbon in the squeeze

67
00:02:50,114 --> 00:02:52,913
video, which squeezing
could not make any more

68
00:02:52,994 --> 00:02:53,713
crowded.

69
00:02:53,954 --> 00:02:56,673
So for carbon plus
carbon dioxide making two

70
00:02:56,754 --> 00:03:00,433
carbon monoxide, K is the
carbon monoxide squared

71
00:03:00,594 --> 00:03:03,473
over the carbon dioxide,
and the carbon never

72
00:03:03,594 --> 00:03:04,113
appears.

73
00:03:04,674 --> 00:03:07,313
If water is a gas, as steam, its

74
00:03:07,394 --> 00:03:09,873
concentration changes, so it counts.

75
00:03:11,100 --> 00:03:12,820
What does the number tell us?

76
00:03:13,100 --> 00:03:16,460
K is products over
reactants, so the bigger

77
00:03:16,540 --> 00:03:18,860
it is, the more the settled mixture leans

78
00:03:18,900 --> 00:03:20,220
towards products.

79
00:03:20,540 --> 00:03:22,700
As a rough guide, a K above about

80
00:03:22,780 --> 00:03:25,340
a thousand means the mixture
at equilibrium is

81
00:03:25,420 --> 00:03:28,140
mostly products, and a K below about a

82
00:03:28,180 --> 00:03:30,900
thousandth means it is mostly reactants.

83
00:03:31,180 --> 00:03:34,340
In between, both are present
in measurable amounts.

84
00:03:34,700 --> 00:03:36,380
It is only a rough guide, because it

85
00:03:36,580 --> 00:03:37,660
depends on the equation.

86
00:03:38,300 --> 00:03:40,460
Hydrogen and iodine at
four hundred and fifty

87
00:03:40,540 --> 00:03:44,060
degrees have a K
of forty-nine: in between,

88
00:03:44,140 --> 00:03:46,380
so our tube holds a lot of hydrogen

89
00:03:46,460 --> 00:03:49,180
iodide, with some
hydrogen and iodine left.

90
00:03:49,820 --> 00:03:52,700
Nitrogen and oxygen
making nitric oxide have a

91
00:03:52,780 --> 00:03:54,700
K near ten to the minus thirty at

92
00:03:54,780 --> 00:03:58,300
room temperature, so almost
no nitric oxide forms.

93
00:03:58,940 --> 00:04:01,340
Copper ions with plenty of ammonia make a

94
00:04:01,500 --> 00:04:03,500
deep blue ion with a K near ten

95
00:04:03,580 --> 00:04:06,460
to the thirteen, so almost all the copper

96
00:04:06,580 --> 00:04:07,820
ends up in that ion.

97
00:04:08,460 --> 00:04:11,020
K tells you where the mixture settles, not

98
00:04:11,100 --> 00:04:12,620
how fast it gets there.

99
00:04:13,834 --> 00:04:16,473
Here is a shortcut for
writing any expression.

100
00:04:16,954 --> 00:04:22,073
Products over reactants, coefficients
become powers, pure solids,

101
00:04:22,154 --> 00:04:24,713
a pure liquid and the solvent drop out.

102
00:04:25,934 --> 00:04:26,573
Your turn.

103
00:04:27,214 --> 00:04:30,413
Two settled mixtures, each
at a steady temperature.

104
00:04:30,894 --> 00:04:34,493
One: in dilute aqueous
solution, copper two plus

105
00:04:34,654 --> 00:04:37,693
ions and ammonia make a deep blue ion.

106
00:04:38,174 --> 00:04:39,853
Write the equilibrium expression.

107
00:04:40,494 --> 00:04:44,253
Two: a made-up reaction
in dilute aqueous solution,

108
00:04:44,374 --> 00:04:47,213
where A and B make C and D,

109
00:04:47,294 --> 00:04:48,573
each with a one in front.

110
00:04:49,054 --> 00:04:50,013
Write the expression.

111
00:04:50,574 --> 00:04:53,133
We start with equal
concentrations of A and

112
00:04:53,214 --> 00:04:55,133
B, and no C or D.

113
00:04:55,694 --> 00:04:57,853
In this question K is four.

114
00:04:58,414 --> 00:05:00,013
What does that tell you about the settled

115
00:05:00,054 --> 00:05:00,773
mixture?

116
00:05:01,054 --> 00:05:02,253
Pause here to answer.

117
00:05:12,667 --> 00:05:13,066
One.

118
00:05:13,227 --> 00:05:16,426
Products on top, reactants underneath.

119
00:05:16,667 --> 00:05:18,266
The new ion goes on top.

120
00:05:18,667 --> 00:05:21,546
Underneath goes the copper
ion times the ammonia

121
00:05:21,587 --> 00:05:23,946
to the power of four,
because the coefficient

122
00:05:24,107 --> 00:05:25,546
four becomes a power.

123
00:05:26,107 --> 00:05:28,986
If you wrote four times
the ammonia, remember

124
00:05:29,227 --> 00:05:32,586
a coefficient is a power,
not a multiplier.

125
00:05:32,907 --> 00:05:35,786
If you added the concentrations
underneath, remember the

126
00:05:35,947 --> 00:05:39,226
iron tube: multiplying
them gave a tenth both

127
00:05:39,307 --> 00:05:41,386
times, adding would not.

128
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:43,200
Two.

129
00:05:43,400 --> 00:05:46,560
The products go on top, C times D.

130
00:05:46,840 --> 00:05:50,280
Underneath go the reactants, A times B.

131
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:52,920
We started with only A and B, in

132
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:53,800
equal amounts.

133
00:05:54,280 --> 00:05:56,200
A K of four works out to about

134
00:05:56,280 --> 00:05:58,680
two thirds of the A reacting, so the

135
00:05:58,840 --> 00:06:02,120
settled mixture holds
measurable amounts of all four,

136
00:06:02,240 --> 00:06:03,960
not almost all products.

137
00:06:05,167 --> 00:06:07,726
So when a question
gives an equation, write

138
00:06:07,807 --> 00:06:11,566
products over reactants, give
each concentration the power

139
00:06:11,607 --> 00:06:14,446
of its coefficient,
and leave out pure solids,

140
00:06:14,527 --> 00:06:16,926
a pure liquid and the solvent.

141
00:06:17,007 --> 00:06:19,246
When it gives you K, read its size

142
00:06:19,407 --> 00:06:22,206
first, as a rough guide: above about a

143
00:06:22,247 --> 00:06:26,206
thousand, mostly products,
below about a thousandth, mostly

144
00:06:26,407 --> 00:06:30,326
reactants, and in between,
both in measurable amounts.

145
00:06:30,767 --> 00:06:33,966
Next: when you only know
the starting amounts,

146
00:06:34,047 --> 00:06:35,806
how do you find the settled mixture?

147
00:06:37,034 --> 00:06:38,473
Here are the key notes.

148
00:06:38,714 --> 00:06:40,553
Pause the video if you need more time

149
00:06:40,634 --> 00:06:41,433
to copy them.
